## 1. Why I selected this opening

The larger scientific objective is reliable intervention: knowing what will happen when we alter a system, even when most of that system is inaccessible or too complicated to reconstruct.

The baseline comparison ruled out several easy claims.

**Rare-event prediction already has strong constructive methods.** Learned committors and transition-path sampling have substantial implementations and applications. One recent protein–ligand study reports recovering kinetics across systems spanning roughly 17 orders of magnitude in residence time; its code and supplementary data are available. That made another generic committor or variational-rate construction a weak choice without a distinct missing operation. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="0"}

**Nonlinear response without a complete microscopic model is also established.** Müller, Basu, Sollich and Krüger show how weak active measurements of coarse path weights can determine second-order response, including time-dependent perturbations and situations without a separation of timescales. Their method acquires information through perturbation experiments. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="1"}

**Dynamical reweighting is a serious comparator.** Girsanov methods provide likelihood-based relations between changed dynamics when the required microscopic quantities are available. Recent marginal Girsanov work addresses the variance growth of long trajectories, with an implementation deposited on Zenodo. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="2"}

**Control through short native simulations predates this work.** Equation-free computation already uses appropriately initialized microscopic simulations to obtain quantities needed for feedback control. Local error analysis for split stochastic dynamics is likewise established. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="3"}

The opening that survived was more precise:

> **Acquire or synthesize the particular local generator operation needed by an intervention, while retaining the exterior system in its actual conditional native state.**

